### 2. Admin requests swap: their Amphi 1000 (500 students) → Bob's COLTECH 101 (60 students)
# Note: this doesn't match the "requester > target student count" rule... but
# the rule requires REQUESTER's class to be LARGER than target's, which IS true here
# (500 > 60). Swap ID needs the actual booking IDs from setup responses.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/swaps
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requesterBookingId": "688617f3-b0d8-46be-80ca-90468f647898",
  "targetBookingId": "PASTE_BOB_BOOKING_ID"
}

### 3. Bob sees incoming swap
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/swaps/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### 4. Bob accepts the swap
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/swaps/PASTE_SWAP_ID/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### 5. Verify halls swapped: Bob now in Amphi 1000, Admin now in COLTECH 101
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/mine
